// The linter, after eslint. See the commit that introduced this file for why the swap
// happened at all: `@typescript-eslint` peers on `typescript <6.1.0` and oxlint parses
// TypeScript itself, so the linter no longer has an opinion about which compiler ships.
//
// The three rules this package established — `no-unused-vars` with `^_`, `no-console`,
// `eqeqeq` — moved to the repository root in #690, where the web editor and the docs site
// now inherit them too. They are unchanged, only relocated; this package was the one with
// a track record and the root file is that track record written down once.
//
// The `correctness` category is likewise stated at the root now rather than left implicit.
// It is 71 rules rather than 3, this source passed all of it unmodified, and the coverage
// stays on for the same reason it was never turned off.
{
  "extends": ["../../../.oxlintrc.json"],
  "overrides": [
    // `no-console` is off here and only here — the same exception `eslint.config.mjs` made,
    // for the same reason. These scripts are run by a person or by CI and their output IS
    // the result: a packaging check that cannot say what is wrong with the package has not
    // checked anything.
    //
    // `scripts/` needed its own block under eslint because it was otherwise parsed as
    // JavaScript and TypeScript syntax failed on it. That half is gone: oxlint reads every
    // file here as TypeScript, so this override now narrows one rule and nothing else.
    {
      "files": ["scripts/**/*.ts"],
      "rules": {
        "eslint/no-console": "off"
      }
    }
  ]
}
